# Build context exclusions.
#
# Two reasons a path is listed here. The first is size: caches, virtual
# environments and the local SQLite file are large and rebuild reproducibly.
# The second is correctness, and it is the more important one: the image must
# not contain the simulation stack, the test suite, the raw datasets, or the
# developer's database, because each of those either changes what the container
# can do or leaks state into a deployment. Nüst et al. (2020) make the same
# point from the reproducibility side — what is not copied cannot vary between
# builds.

# Version control and tooling metadata
.git
.gitignore
.github
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov
ruff.toml
pytest.ini

# Python environments and bytecode
.venv
.venv.nosync
venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info

# The local database and evidence: deployment state, never an image input
*.db
*.sqlite3
docs/evidence
temp.*

# Raw and large data. data/networks/ is copied explicitly by the Dockerfile
# because the application needs the case network and the 48 h ground truth.
data/raw
data/sim

# Development-only trees that would re-introduce the simulation stack
tests
examples
Unit*

# Editors and OS
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea
